<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade-Aug 18.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade-Aug 18.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended Aug 16</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>SCRIP		 SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA   QTY    VALUE   % BADLA</p>
<p>			RATE				 (RS MLN)</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Reliance	     370.00	1.11     435400  161.10   15.64</p>
<p>TISCO		  205.00	0.62     681250  139.66   15.77</p>
<p>State Bank	   320.00	0.96     395450  126.54   15.64</p>
<p>Telco		  375.00	1.14     210800   79.05   15.85</p>
<p>G.E.Shipping	  46.00	0.14    1709400   78.63   15.87</p>
<p>BSES		   215.00	0.65     274600   59.04   15.76</p>
<p>Tata Tea	     465.00	1.18     111300   51.75   13.23</p>
<p>Escorts		113.00	0.34     427550   48.31   15.69</p>
<p>ACC		   1565.00	4.75	25640   40.13   15.83</p>
<p>HDFC		  3485.00     10.49	10700   37.29   15.70</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 15.75 percent on an annualised basis against 17.75 percent in the previous carry forward account ended Aug 9.</p>
<p>Note :- BC - Book Closure</p>
